On my way up with The Amulet I often fill the remaining trapdoors
in the Castle with boulders to (kind of) seal Gehennom so that no
unaware fellow accidentally enters that horrible place.[*]

Today I noticed that The Wizard used the same word *immediately*
after I've done that sealing. (The comment on line 3 was written
for the NAO audience.)

With great effort you move the boulder.
The boulder triggers and plugs a trap door in the floor!
#  Gehennom is sealed now
A voice booms out...  "So thou thought thou couldst kill me, fool."
[...the usual fight messages snipped...]
The Wizard of Yendor points at you, then curses.
"Thy fate is sealed, fool!"

A nice coincidence (speaking of sealing), and good a timing of the
Wizard's appearance - not that it was of any use to him, though. ;-}

Janis

[*] That's just for, hmm.., say, style or atmosphere; has nothing
to do with the game.


